+  // (mitcad#2415) A seam is an edge the face has twice, once each way. An
+  // edge where the face meets a tangent face along the line of its seam (a
+  // flat side tangent to a cylinder where the cylinder's seam lies, the
+  // seam split there by a fuse) may keep both curves of the seam on the
+  // surface though the face has it once: taken for a seam, it made two
+  // seams here, and the offset of theV was put on the offset of the
+  // tangential edge, which then ran on past the faces cutting it (the
+  // offset of the flat side was not built).
+  const bool bSeam1 = BRepTools::IsReallyClosed(theE1, theF);
+  const bool bSeam2 = BRepTools::IsReallyClosed(theE2, theF);
   if (bSeam1 == bSeam2)
   {
     return false;
